      ],
      "blind_answer": 1,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "The PvuI site lies in the amp^R gene of pBR322. An insert there inactivates ampicillin resistance while tet^R stays intact, so recombinants grow on tetracycline but not on ampicillin."
    },
    {
      "q_id": "neet_bio_u09_t00_4",
      "published": true,
      "reason": null,
      "manual_approved": false,
      "our_answer": [
        2
      ],
      "blind_answer": 2,
      "confidence": "high",
      "blind_working": "The BamHI site lies in tet^R. An insert there inactivates tetracycline resistance, so A is true. pBR322 does carry ori and rop, so R is true, but R does not explain A."
    },
    {
      "q_id": "neet_bio_u09_t00_5",
      "published": true,
      "reason": null,
      "manual_approved": false,
      "our_answer": [
